// =============================================================================
// P02 — GOVERN & CONTROL
// Agentic AI Security Labs | KQL Library
// Target: Microsoft Sentinel / Defender Advanced Hunting
// Tables: AgentsInfo, AuditLogs, CloudAppEvents, PowerPlatformAdminActivity
// SCHEMA NOTES (verified live against tenant AgentsInfo via pack_all(), Sep 2026):
//   AgentsInfo.Name | Owners: dynamic, can be null
//   EntraAgentID (capital D at the end) | Both Timestamp and TimeGenerated exist
//   AgentsInfo.Timestamp is the daily snapshot of the inventory, not agent activity. Owners are user object ids.
// Re-run on 2026-10-05: Q1 and Q3 in Advanced Hunting (real AgentsInfo), Q4 on a Sentinel workspace (real AuditLogs).
//      Q2, Q5 and Q6 have no source data on the validation tenant and stay NOT VERIFIED.
// =============================================================================


// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Q1: Agents Without Entra Agent ID — Identity Orphans
// Use: Find agents with no dedicated Entra agent identity, split by whether a blueprint exists
//      NoEntraIdentity: neither EntraAgentID nor EntraBlueprintID -> identity laundering risk
//      BlueprintOnly:   a blueprint exists but no agent identity in this tenant -> confirm how it authenticates
//      (agents with an EntraAgentID are excluded; they have a dedicated identity)
//      NoEntraIdentity also covers Copilot Studio agents created before May 2026 (an app registration, not an
//      agent identity) and Agent Builder agents (no identity properties): confirm before calling it laundering.
// Validated live (Oct 2026, Advanced Hunting): runs without errors against the real AgentsInfo.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
AgentsInfo
| where Timestamp > ago(30d)
| where isempty(EntraAgentID)
| extend OwnersStr = tostring(Owners)
| extend OwnerDisplay = iff(OwnersStr == "" or OwnersStr == "[]", "UNASSIGNED", OwnersStr)
| extend IdentityState = iff(isnotempty(EntraBlueprintID), "BlueprintOnly", "NoEntraIdentity")
| distinct AgentId, Name, Platform, OwnerDisplay, IdentityState, LifecycleStatus, PublishedStatus
| extend RiskNote = iff(IdentityState == "NoEntraIdentity",
    "No Entra identity: no agent identity and no blueprint — identity laundering risk",
    "Blueprint only: no agent identity in this tenant — confirm how the agent authenticates")
| sort by IdentityState desc, Platform asc


// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Q2: Copilot Studio Agents Created, Published or Shared — Maker Activity
// Use: List who created, published or shared Copilot Studio agents, so that each one can be checked against your
//      approval process. The governance gap behind it: agents that reach users without a review step.
// Note: Two paths (Microsoft Learn, July 2026): sharing an Agent Builder agent has no admin review and applies updates
//      at once; submitting it to the organization catalog (Agent Store) requires admin approval in the Microsoft 365
//      admin center. The gap this query is about is the sharing path.
// Source: Copilot Studio authoring events are Power Platform administrator activity in the Purview audit log
//      (Microsoft Learn, "Audit Copilot Studio activities in Microsoft Purview"): BotCreate,
//      BotUpdateOperation-BotPublish and BotUpdateOperation-BotShare. In Sentinel they arrive through the "Microsoft
//      Power Platform Admin Activity" connector, table PowerPlatformAdminActivity, with the operation in
//      EventOriginalType. Learn's sample-queries page for that table still shows the old name
//      PowerPlatformAdministratorActivity, which does not resolve.
// Approval: no Copilot Studio event records an approval, so "without approval" cannot be read from these events
//      alone: compare each publish or share with your approval record. An admin approval of an org-catalog
//      submission is DeployedAgent in the Microsoft 365 admin center agent management activities (Purview audit log).
//      No audit operation for sharing an Agent Builder agent is documented in the Learn pages reviewed (Oct 2026):
//      after sharing one, search the Purview audit log for the maker and the time, and note the operation name.
// NOT VERIFIED (live tenant, Oct 2026): PowerPlatformAdminActivity exists in the validation workspace, with the
//      columns Learn lists, but has no rows (the Power Platform connectors are not ingesting), and no OfficeActivity
//      operation matching Bot, Copilot, Agent or Plugin exists in 180 days. The query compiles; the operation names
//      and the keys inside Properties were not seen on live events.
// Not a source for this: CopilotActivity. Its CopilotAgentManagement record (one in the workspace) names a Microsoft
//      first-party agent and shares its second with a CopilotForSecurityTrigger record, which points to Security
//      Copilot agent management (Learn lists CreateCopilotAgent, UpdateCopilotAgent and DeleteCopilotAgent for it).
//      The record carries no operation, so create, update and delete cannot be told apart, and it is not Copilot Studio
//      or Agent Builder.
// The earlier version read AuditLogs for "AgentPublished", an operation that does not exist in Entra audit logs.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
PowerPlatformAdminActivity
| where TimeGenerated > ago(30d)
| where EventOriginalType in (
    "BotCreate",
    "BotUpdateOperation-BotPublish",
    "BotUpdateOperation-BotShare")
| where EventResult == "Succeeded"
| project
    TimeGenerated,
    EventOriginalType,
    ActorName,
    ActorUserType,
    EnvironmentId,
    EventResult,
    Properties
| sort by TimeGenerated desc


// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Q3: Agents Without Lifecycle Review — Not Changed in Months
// Use: Identify active agents that nobody has changed or published in the review window
//      Signals candidates for decommission review
// Validated live (Oct 2026, Advanced Hunting): the earlier version took max(Timestamp) as "last activity", but
//      AgentsInfo.Timestamp is the daily snapshot, so every agent reported 0 days and the query returned nothing.
//      It now uses the agent's own last change (LastUpdatedDateTime, LastPublishedDateTime, CreatedDateTime) on the
//      latest snapshot: 195 of the active agents were last changed more than 60 days ago, 78 of them more than 180.
//      This measures the last change, not usage: an unchanged agent can still be in daily use. AgentsInfo has no
//      activity column, so a usage-based review needs CloudAppEvents (InvokeAgent) once it carries data.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
AgentsInfo
| where Timestamp > ago(30d)
| summarize arg_max(Timestamp, *) by AgentId
| where LifecycleStatus == "Active"
| extend OwnersStr = tostring(Owners)
| extend OwnerDisplay = iff(OwnersStr == "" or OwnersStr == "[]", "UNASSIGNED", OwnersStr)
| extend LastChange = max_of(LastUpdatedDateTime, LastPublishedDateTime, CreatedDateTime)
| extend DaysSinceChange = datetime_diff('day', now(), LastChange)
| where DaysSinceChange > 60
| extend LifecycleRisk = case(
    DaysSinceChange > 180, "Critical — exceeds 6-month review window",
    DaysSinceChange > 90,  "High — exceeds 3-month review window",
    "Medium — approaching review threshold"
)
| sort by DaysSinceChange desc
| project AgentId, Name, Platform, OwnerDisplay, LastChange, DaysSinceChange, LifecycleRisk


// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Q4: Graph Drift Detection — Agents With Accumulating Permissions
// Use: Identify agents whose permission scope has expanded over time
//      without corresponding approval events
// NOT VERIFIED (live tenant, Oct 2026): the grant side uses real Entra operations. The approval side
//      ("AgentPermissionApproved") is not confirmed to exist, so as written EVERY grant is reported as
//      "without approval". Use it as an inventory of grants, not as proof of a missing approval.
// Validated live (Oct 2026, Sentinel workspace, grant side): the earlier version read TargetResources[0] as the
//      agent and modifiedProperties[0] as the permission. In these events TargetResources[0] is the resource that
//      receives the grant and TargetResources[1] is the client service principal; the permission is in the property
//      DelegatedPermissionGrant.Scope (delegated) or AppRole.Value (application), and modifiedProperties[0] is the
//      app role id or a different property. 28 grants in 30 days now come back with permission, client and
//      initiator populated (initiator falls back to the app when no user started it).
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
AuditLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(30d)
| where OperationName in ("Add delegated permission grant", "Add app role assignment to service principal")
| extend ResourceName = tostring(TargetResources[0].displayName)
| extend AgentObjectId = tostring(TargetResources[1].id)
| mv-apply MP = TargetResources[0].modifiedProperties on (
    where tostring(MP.displayName) in ("DelegatedPermissionGrant.Scope", "AppRole.Value")
    | summarize NewPermission = take_any(tostring(MP.newValue)))
| extend GrantedBy = coalesce(tostring(InitiatedBy.user.userPrincipalName), tostring(InitiatedBy.app.displayName))
| join kind=leftouter (
    AuditLogs
    | where OperationName == "AgentPermissionApproved"
    | distinct CorrelationId
) on CorrelationId
| where isempty(CorrelationId1)
| project
    TimeGenerated,
    AgentObjectId,
    ResourceName,
    NewPermission,
    GrantedBy,
    RiskNote = "Permission granted without corresponding approval event"
| sort by TimeGenerated desc


// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Q5: Maker Activity — Power Platform Agents Without DLP Policy Coverage
// Use: Detect agents created by makers using connectors outside DLP boundaries
// NOT VERIFIED (live tenant, Oct 2026): CloudAppEvents has no "Microsoft Power Platform" application events in the
//      validation tenant, and "AgentConnectorAdded" and the RawEventData fields (ConnectorName, DLPClassification)
//      are not documented, so the query was not run against live events. Treat it as a template: Power Platform
//      maker and connector activity is documented in the Purview audit log, not under this ActionType.
//      Learn's Sentinel solution for Power Platform reads connector creation and DLP policy changes from
//      PowerPlatformAdminActivity (built-in rules "Power Platform - Connector added to a sensitive environment" and
//      "Power Platform - DLP policy updated or removed"); that table exists in the validation workspace and has no rows.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CloudAppEvents
| where Timestamp > ago(30d)
| where Application == "Microsoft Power Platform"
    and ActionType == "AgentConnectorAdded"
| extend ConnectorName = tostring(RawEventData["ConnectorName"])
| extend ConnectorClassification = tostring(RawEventData["DLPClassification"])
| where ConnectorClassification == "NonBusiness"
    or isempty(ConnectorClassification)
| summarize
    ConnectorUses = count(),
    LastUsed = max(Timestamp),
    Makers = make_set(AccountDisplayName)
    by ConnectorName, ConnectorClassification
| sort by ConnectorUses desc
| project ConnectorName, ConnectorClassification, ConnectorUses, LastUsed, Makers


// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Q6: Consent Architecture Gap — Compound Actions Without Per-Step HITL Events
// Use: Identify agent sessions that executed multi-action sequences
//      (read + write + send) without corresponding per-action consent/approval events
//      Signals missing HITL gates for compound actions — consent architecture gap
// Reference: Microsoft AIRT Taxonomy v2.0 §5.4 | Tiered Autonomy principle
// Recommended: Weekly scheduled query or Analytics Rule | Severity: Medium
// NOT VERIFIED (live tenant, Oct 2026): none of the approval events (AgentActionApproved,
//      AgentConsentGranted, AgentStepApproved, UserApprovedAgentAction) is confirmed to exist in
//      AuditLogs, and the SessionId / AgentId fields read from CloudAppEvents RawEventData are unverified.
//      As written, every multi-action session would be reported. Treat it as a design sketch. AdditionalDetails
//      is an array of {key, value} objects in AuditLogs, so AdditionalDetails["SessionId"] returns empty (see Q2).
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
let CompoundActionTypes = dynamic([
    "FileDownloaded", "FileCopied", "FileUploaded",
    "MessageSent", "EmailSent", "MeetingCreated",
    "RecordCreated", "RecordUpdated", "RecordDeleted"
]);
let ApprovalEvents = AuditLogs
    | where TimeGenerated > ago(7d)
    | where OperationName in (
        "AgentActionApproved", "AgentConsentGranted",
        "AgentStepApproved", "UserApprovedAgentAction"
    )
    | extend SessionId = tostring(AdditionalDetails["SessionId"])
    | distinct SessionId;
CloudAppEvents
| where TimeGenerated > ago(7d)
| where ActionType in (CompoundActionTypes)
| extend SessionId = tostring(RawEventData["SessionId"])
| extend AgentId = tostring(RawEventData["AgentId"])
| where isnotempty(SessionId) and isnotempty(AgentId)
| summarize
    ActionsInSession = count(),
    DistinctActionTypes = dcount(ActionType),
    ActionSequence = make_set(ActionType),
    LastAction = max(TimeGenerated),
    AccountDisplayName = any(AccountDisplayName)
    by SessionId, AgentId
| where DistinctActionTypes >= 2   // Compound action: at least 2 distinct action types
| join kind=leftanti ApprovalEvents on SessionId
| extend RiskNote = strcat(
    "Agent executed ", DistinctActionTypes, " distinct action types in session without HITL consent events — ",
    "compound action decomposition may be missing"
)
| project
    SessionId, AgentId, AccountDisplayName,
    ActionsInSession, DistinctActionTypes,
    ActionSequence, LastAction, RiskNote
| sort by DistinctActionTypes desc, ActionsInSession desc
